# Cloudflare Pages headers file. Has no effect locally — Pages applies it at the
# edge. Syntax: a path pattern on its own line, then indented "Name: value" lines.
#
# ⚠️ STRUCTURE: the CSP is deliberately NOT on /* any more. Several pages carry
# different policies (⚠️ 2026-08-15: /todo no longer "must never gain JS" — see
# its own section below, kept for the historical record), and a
# path that matched two CSP rules could end up with two CSP headers — which
# browsers enforce as the INTERSECTION, silently breaking sign-in. So /* carries
# only the non-CSP safety headers, and each page's CSP lives on its own exact
# rules. A NEW page added under public/ therefore ships with NO CSP until a rule
# is added here — add one, strict by default, in the same commit as the page.
#
# ⚠️ TRAILING SLASH, discovered 2026-08-14 building /status: Pages 308s a
# subdirectory request from its bare form ("/admin") to the trailing-slash
# form ("/admin/") before serving the file, and a _headers path pattern
# matches ONLY the exact request path — "/admin" does NOT also match
# "/admin/". The 308 itself carries the CSP (it matched), but the redirect's
# empty body is never rendered, so the browser applies whatever headers
# arrive on the FINAL 200 — which had none. Net effect: /admin and /todo have
# been serving their real page with **no CSP at all** since each was added;
# only curling the bare path (which the deploy checklists happen to do)
# looked like proof it worked. Fixed here by adding an explicit
# trailing-slash duplicate of every subdirectory rule; a future page under
# public/<name>/ needs both "/<name>" and "/<name>/" for this reason.
#
# THE FRONT DOOR + /admin POLICY (estate-auth-design.md §7.2 — the old
# "zero external requests" rule was overturned WITH the reasoning on record;
# the in-file comment atop index.html carries it). Allow-listed, not open:
#   script-src  'self' + www.gstatic.com (Firebase SDK modules, the same CDN
#               builds every audiobook page ships) + apis.google.com (the
#               sign-in popup's helper — Google-controlled, needed by some
#               popup flows; remove if observed unused).
#   connect-src the two estate Workers (index = search, auth = the /admin
#               API whose CORS names exactly https://heygabi.ai) + Firebase
#               auth endpoints (identitytoolkit = sign-in, securetoken =
#               token refresh). /admin ONLY additionally names the THREE app
#               Workers (library, boardgames, and — 2026-08-16 —
#               padhard.heygabi.ai, "Sam's library") — the federated role
#               columns read/write each app's own /api/admin surface, whose
#               CORS is locked to this origin; the front door has no business
#               there, so its rule does not carry them.
#               ⚠️ CSP IS THE SECOND LOCK, AND IT FAILS DIFFERENTLY FROM THE
#               FIRST. padhard's own CORS was correct from the day it
#               deployed (same Worker code as library.heygabi.ai), and the
#               role column STILL read "unreachable" until this line named
#               it: a blocked fetch() REJECTS in the page, which
#               fetchAppDirectory() cannot tell apart from a dead host. So
#               adding a federated app is TWO edits — the APPS row in
#               admin.js and this host — and shipping only the first looks
#               exactly like the other site being down.
#   frame-src   the Firebase auth iframe on the project's authDomain, and
#               accounts.google.com for the sign-in flow. Widened 2026-08-16
#               (sso-design.md §4.1/§8 Phase 1) to ALSO name
#               https://auth.heygabi.ai, alongside the firebaseapp.com entry
#               kept through the transition — estate-auth.js's authDomain now
#               points there (auth.heygabi.ai reverse-proxies /__/auth/* to
#               audiobook-catalog.firebaseapp.com), and the /admin rule below
#               carries the same addition for the same reason.
#   img-src     'self' data: (the inline SVG favicon) + the estate's cover
#               hosts: covers.heygabi.ai (audiobook), bookcovers.heygabi.ai +
#               library.heygabi.ai (library), gamecovers.heygabi.ai (games).
#               PRUNED 2026-08-15: games' third-party tail (cf.geekdo-images
#               .com and the shopify/gamefound/dndbeyond/dicethrone/
#               cloudfront/squarespace/kickstarter/itch/loottavern/d20/
#               backerkit/bigcommerce hosts, MEASURED 2026-08-14 from the
#               2,259 production rows) is GONE — the covers consolidation
#               (catalog-platform/docs/info/covers-consolidation-plan.md)
#               rehosted all 1,124 distinct URLs (item.thumbnail_url ∪
#               edition.image_url) onto gamecovers.heygabi.ai, verified
#               against production D1: 0 of 506 item rows and 1 of 974
#               edition rows (a 7.27MB file over the upload ceiling, left as
#               its original hotlink on purpose) still point at a
#               third-party host. This is why estate hosts are named
#               individually rather than a https: wildcard: a missing one
#               silently blanks a thumbnail (find.js keeps the slot, drops
#               the broken image) rather than breaking loudly, so the list
#               has to stay exactly what production actually serves. Plus
#               Google avatars.
#   style-src   'self' (assets/estate-theme.css — the theme system) +
#               'unsafe-inline' for the per-page <style> blocks; with inline
#               SCRIPT still blocked there is no injection vector to
#               leverage a nonce against (unchanged reasoning).
#   font-src    'self' ONLY — every theme font (Rajdhani, Share Tech Mono,
#               Bangers, Luckiest Guy) is a committed woff2 under
#               assets/fonts/, the same no-third-party reasoning the games
#               repo used when it committed its own. Google Fonts hosts stay
#               OFF this list on purpose.
# Still absolutely absent: analytics, third-party font requests, CDN frameworks.
#
# /todo — SUPERSEDED 2026-08-15 (owner order: "Auth lock the todo page too").
# The line this comment used to carry — "/todo KEEPS THE ORIGINAL
# default-src 'none' NO-JS POLICY... the strict CSP is the enforcement of
# that sentence" — kept the page from acquiring a <script>, but the page was
# still PUBLIC: every board item shipped in cleartext to anyone who
# requested the URL, JS or no JS. That protected against the wrong thing —
# a hidden link, not a lock. The board's content moved OFF this origin
# entirely, into the auth Worker (apps/auth-worker/src/todo-board.ts, served
# by requireApprover()-gated GET /api/estate/todo); this page is now a
# content-free shim that signs in and fetches the board only after the
# Worker answers 200. The CSS-only radio filter is UNCHANGED — still no JS
# in the filtering itself, only in the sign-in + fetch — so the rule below
# is the SAME sign-in allow-list shape as /status's Operations section, not
# a general loosening:
#   script-src  'self' (this page's own /todo/todo.js module) +
#               www.gstatic.com (Firebase SDK) + apis.google.com (the
#               sign-in popup helper).
#   connect-src auth.heygabi.ai (GET /api/estate/todo, CORS locked to this
#               apex — apps/auth-worker/src/index.ts) +
#               identitytoolkit.googleapis.com + securetoken.googleapis.com
#               (sign-in + token refresh).
#   frame-src   the Firebase auth iframe on the project's authDomain, and
#               accounts.google.com for the popup/redirect flow — same two
#               hosts as every other estate-auth page on this site.
#   img-src     unchanged: 'self' data: only (the inline SVG favicon; the
#               board carries no images).
#   style-src   unchanged: 'unsafe-inline' only — still one inline <style>
#               block, no external stylesheet link, so 'self' is not needed.
#
# /status (added 2026-08-14, the estate status page — "I want to see all the
# pipelines"). connect-src names exactly the seven hosts status.js fetches: the
# five /api/health origins it reads as JSON (index/auth/library/games, plus
# padhard.heygabi.ai — "Sam's library" — added 2026-08-16 with its worker and
# site rows; her deploy is separate from ours even though the code is shared,
# so a green library row says nothing about hers), the
# audiobook site root (whose /dev/ lane AND /ebooks.json are checked at the
# same origin, so neither needs a separate entry), and — added 2026-08-15
# for the Book pipeline row — firestore.googleapis.com, read over the plain
# REST API for the one public document pipeline_status/current (no Firebase
# SDK needed or added for THAT row: a signed-out GET is enough, same as every
# other read-only row). No img-src beyond the inline SVG favicon — this page
# renders no covers. form-action and base-uri stay 'none'.
#
# Operations (added 2026-08-15, "make sure the status page has all the
# pieces to RUN the pipelines"): the page's read-only rows still need no
# sign-in, but the new Operations section does, so this rule now ALSO
# carries the front door's sign-in trio — script-src gains www.gstatic.com
# (Firebase SDK) + apis.google.com (the popup helper); connect-src gains
# identitytoolkit.googleapis.com + securetoken.googleapis.com (sign-in +
# token refresh — auth.heygabi.ai was ALREADY here for the Workers row
# above, so the one new REST call this section makes, POST
# /api/estate/ops/pipeline, needed no new host); frame-src, 'none' on every
# other rule on this page, now names the project's authDomain + Google's
# accounts page for the popup/redirect flow, same as / and /admin.
#
# /universes (added 2026-08-15, one row per estate universe expanding to
# /api/universe/:name). Signs in (universes.js reuses estate-auth.js), so it
# carries the front door's script-src (Firebase SDK) and frame-src (the
# popup/redirect sign-in flow), but connect-src drops auth.heygabi.ai — this
# page shows no admin surface and never calls that Worker. img-src is the
# SAME cover-host allow-list as the front door's own "/" rule below, copied
# verbatim rather than hand-maintained separately, because a universe's rows
# can carry a cover from any source the estate indexes (audiobook, library or
# game) — read that list fresh before editing either one; a copy that drifts
# from "/" is how a cover host silently blanks here but not there.
#
# /series (added 2026-08-17, one row per registry series expanding to
# /api/series/:slug — the volume-by-volume view with the GAP rows). Signs in
# (series.js imports estate-auth.js directly, same as universes.js), so it
# carries the front door's script-src (Firebase SDK) and frame-src (the
# popup/redirect sign-in flow).
#   connect-src ⚠️ index.heygabi.ai IS THE WHOLE PAGE. Both of its fetches go
#               there and nowhere else, and a CSP-blocked fetch() REJECTS in
#               the page — series.js's own catch() would then report "the
#               index did not answer (network)", which is indistinguishable
#               from the Worker being down. That is the exact miss that cost
#               an evening on /admin's role columns the day before (see the
#               connect-src note above and estate-auth-design.md §1.2), so it
#               is named here first. Plus identitytoolkit + securetoken for
#               sign-in and token refresh. NOT named, because this page does
#               not call them: auth.heygabi.ai (no admin surface),
#               openlibrary.org and 'self' (no <estate-search scan> here —
#               the scanner's wasm fetch and ISBN resolve live on / and
#               /universes), library.heygabi.ai (no barcode intake).
#   script-src  no 'wasm-unsafe-eval' for the same reason — no scanner, so
#               nothing on this page compiles WebAssembly.
#   img-src     the SAME cover-host allow-list as "/" — a series' volumes can
#               carry a cover from any source the estate indexes. Read that
#               list fresh before editing either; a copy that drifts is how a
#               cover host silently blanks here but not there.
#   frame-src   names https://auth.heygabi.ai ALONGSIDE the firebaseapp.com
#               entry, matching "/" and /admin rather than /universes.
#               estate-auth.js's authDomain is auth.heygabi.ai as of the SSO
#               Phase 1 cutover (sso-design.md §4.1), so the iframe this page
#               needs is served from there; /universes' rule predates that
