#               vendored — see assets/estate-scan.js's header) would
#               otherwise fail SILENTLY under this CSP with no console error
#               naming the cause. Supported Safari 16+ / Chrome 97+ / Firefox
#               102+ — fine for the owner's iPhone.
#   connect-src gains 'self' (the same-origin fetch() of assets/scanner/
#               zxing_reader.wasm — governed by connect-src, not script-src,
#               because it is a network fetch rather than a script load) and
#               https://openlibrary.org (the two-fetch ISBN→title/author
#               resolve, assets/estate-scan.js's resolveIsbn()). img-src
#               already carries https://covers.openlibrary.org on both pages
#               from the cover-host list above — no change needed there.
#               ALSO gains https://library.heygabi.ai — the "Add to Books →"
#               affordance (owner: "add it from the main page to the right
#               catalog") POSTs a resolved ISBN to the library app's own
#               barcode-intake endpoint with the signed-in member's bearer
#               token; the library Worker's own CORS must separately allow
#               this origin (library_catalog repo, tracked there).
#   Permissions-Policy (on /*, below): camera=() → camera=(self) — see that
#   rule's own comment.

