# Cache-Control on everything (2026-08-15, owner: "can we make giving roles
# hard refresh or something?"): a devops grant looked broken because the
# grantee's browser kept running the PREVIOUS deploy's scripts from cache.
# max-age=0 + must-revalidate makes every asset revalidate on each use —
# Pages' ETags turn that into cheap 304s, so the cost is one conditional
# request per file and the win is that every deploy AND every role change
# is live on a PLAIN reload, never a hard refresh. This site is a handful
# of small files; if a large rarely-changing asset class ever appears,
# carve it out with its own longer rule rather than weakening this one.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(self), interest-cohort=()
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

